; CultivatedWheatRow — one of 2 Cultivated field terrain variants. FIRST REAL ASSET for
; this terrain (2026-08-16); previously a grey-box placeholder. Human complaint: "needs to
; look like actual farm fields." Composes a small wheat plot, not a single plant in a box.
;
; Source: Wheat.glb, "Wheat" by Quaternius, CC0 1.0 Universal, poly.pizza — see
; project/attribution/sources/quaternius_poly_pizza_nature.tres.
;
; Raw measured AABB: footprint 0.358x0.356, height 1.102 tile-units (very tall relative to
; a tile — similar "taller than a villager" situation the grass picks needed correcting
; on import). Scaled to a target ~0.44-0.46 tile-units tall (scale ~0.40-0.43, mild
; per-instance jitter), a stylized "waist-high wheat" judgment call — FLAG FOR HUMAN
; SIGN-OFF, no GDD number exists for crop height.
;
; 6 clumps arranged as 2 loose rows (furrow idiom, not a grid) across the tile — enough to
; read as a small planted plot without the "single plant in the middle of a box" the task
; brief explicitly called out to avoid, and without over-cluttering the tile (explicit
; "variety without noise" caution).
;
; Slab is a dirt-brown (Color(0.4, 0.28, 0.16, 1)), distinct from every natural terrain's
; green/grey slabs — cultivated field is the one terrain that costs Wood and should read
; as worked soil, not wild ground. FLAG FOR HUMAN SIGN-OFF on the exact tone.
;
; SLAB WIDENED 0.94 -> 1.0 (2026-08-16, human-reported cross-tile seam gap) — same fix,
; same reasoning as CommonTree1.tscn's header. X/Z only, Y (0.2) untouched.
